course: dictionary
lesson: 11396
title: Accommodating: helpful, or making room
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which one is right. Accommodating is one of those words. It can describe a person: an accommodating person is helpful and willing to change plans to suit other people. «The hotel staff were very accommodating when we asked for a later check-out.» The staff changed something to help us, so accommodating means helpful and flexible.
explain: Accommodating can also mean having room for people. «The hall is accommodating 300 guests» tells you the hall has space for 300 guests. Ask yourself: is this a person being kind and flexible, or is a place or thing holding people? The clue words, such as hall, guests or passengers, will tell you.
explain: Accommodating can also mean making changes so something fits a need. «The school is accommodating pupils who use wheelchairs» means the school is changing things so those pupils can get in and join in. Check your meaning by swapping in a simple word, such as helpful or made room for, and see if the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Accommodating is an adjective: accommodating, more accommodating, most accommodating.
fact: «Accommodating» can mean helpful and willing to change plans to suit others.
fact: «Accommodate» can mean having room for people, as in «a bus accommodating 50 passengers», which holds up to 50.
fact: Useful phrases are very accommodating, accommodating to others, and accommodating guests.
fact: Accommodating can also mean making changes so that something fits a need, such as a school making room for every pupil.
exercise: «The shopkeeper was very accommodating and let us pay next week.» What does accommodating mean here? | Closed for the day | Angry and loud | Very tall | *Helpful and willing to change plans
exercise: «The coach can accommodate 50 passengers.» What does accommodate mean here? | Stops at every town | Drives very fast | *Has room for | Sells tickets
exercise: «The hotel was accommodating when our flight was late.» Find and copy the word that tells you what the hotel was like. | flight | late | *accommodating | hotel
test: «The school is accommodating pupils who use wheelchairs.» What does accommodating mean here? | Counting the pupils each morning | Painting the classroom walls | Sending them home early | *Making changes so they can join in
test: «A lift accommodating 8 people holds up to 8.» What is the most people the lift can accommodate? | *8 | 6 | 80 | 10
exam: Which sentence shows someone being accommodating? | «The man refused every change to our plans.» | «The park gate was painted green.» | *«The teacher moved our meeting to suit everyone.» | «The bus was full and very cold.»
